    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d159">

                <pb facs="0327" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg255"/>

                <head>No. 34.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Mr. Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 29,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 28th instant, requesting that inquiries may be made into
                    the circumstances attending the arrest of Mr. James L. White, a naturalized
                    American citizen, who has been for some months imprisoned in Naas jail under the
                    protection of person and property act (Ireland), and I have to state to you that
                    your application is under the consideration of Her Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
